<newsitem itemid="101042" id="root" date="1996-10-07" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Capital H1 pre-tax profits rise 23 percent.</title>
<headline>Capital H1 pre-tax profits rise 23 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 24</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		5.0		    vs 3.7</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.0		    vs 0.8</p>
<p> Pretax		     2.52		   vs 2.04</p>
<p> Net asset value(pence) 193.7		  vs 186.2</p>
<p> Attributable	     2.28		   vs 1.67</p>
<p> Pay date		   Nov 22</p>
<p> Div  registration date Oct 22</p>
<p>Note - Property firm Capital &amp; Regional Properties Plc said it has bought a leisure development scheme at Wolverhampton with an estimated end value of around 15 million stg.</p>
<p>The company also said it expects to see a good increase in net asset value per share at the year end.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
